  "body": {
    "summary": "BKIND votes No. This action asks 9,600,000 ada for a vendor to build a police evidence system for a paying state government. The treasury carries the build and the risk while the vendor keeps the client and the maintenance contract.",
    "rationaleStatement": "Action: treasury withdrawal 72491608dc1a500d38613214069a2bd3b7e9a0e670d5abd7d6374e6bb54fc0e8#0, 9,600,000 ada to the reward account stake1uyyqmz5ae7ct4f26p4t87y2xrrgu7f3e0cpap66zgcnxu0gl7gy6y under the current constitution's guardrails script, fa24fb305126805cf2164c161d852a0e7330cf988f1fe558cf7d4a64. I verified on chain that the action withdraws exactly this amount to that credential, that the credential is a public key and not a script, that the action was published on chain on 21 October 2026 in epoch 662, and that the proposal document hashes to the on-chain anchor, 09e2ef6f02fd53aab203c872f082f888e8c53b383377a13e3b71eb08550be389.\n\nWhat I support. Real adoption on Cardano has value. This team points to a prior deployment on Cardano, its FMS, whose transaction record can be checked on the public leaderboard. The action is milestone gated with an independent assurer, names the Cardano Foundation as administrator, caps spending at a fixed rate with the excess returned, and routes most of any future verification revenue to the treasury. My No is not to the project. It is to the treasury carrying a vendor's commercial build.\n\nA build for a paying client. The proposal states that \"the state government has committed to paying for the Cardano transaction fees resulting from PFMS usage and operating the off-chain deployment infrastructure\", and that \"Trivolve Tech and its subcontractors will receive maintenance fees from the state government under a separate agreement\". The client exists, has committed to pay for operation, and holds a maintenance contract with the vendor. Yet the one time build is placed on the treasury. A company normally builds a product at its own cost and carries the risk. Here the build and the risk move to ada holders while the client relationship and the maintenance revenue stay with the vendor.\n\nA cost basis that is not shown. The budget is given only as work package shares of the total. It names no person months and no rates. The work is built in India, a low cost engineering geography, yet the request is tied to no rate and no quantity of work that would let anyone place it against that cost. The ask is \"9,600,000 ADA over 15 months\", about 2.2 million dollars at the planning rate and capped near 2.9 million. Ada holders are asked to approve a figure they cannot check against the work it pays for.\n\nNo downside risk for the outcome. The schedule releases 1,800,000 ada at kickoff and 2,000,000 ada at each of the next three milestones, 7,800,000 ada or more than 80 percent, before the final 1,800,000 ada at month 15, the only milestone tied to use, \"Sustained Usage\". Milestone gating protects against failure to deliver and against fraud. It does not protect against a system that is built and not used. If use does not follow, the treasury carries the loss and the builder does not.\n\nA custody plan that does not match the credential. Under Article II section 7.6 the proposal describes the receiving address as a multi signature wallet held by the administrator, not staked and delegated to the auto abstain DRep. On chain the 9,600,000 ada is withdrawn to the reward account above, and that account is a public key credential, not a script. On Cardano a multi signature wallet is a script. The account named to receive and hold the funds is controlled by a single key at the protocol level. Whether the administrator moves the funds to a multi signature address after withdrawal cannot be read from the action as submitted.\n\nA justification that cannot be verified. The agreements with the state are not public. The proposal states: \"The PFMS project agreements contain confidential state information and cannot be shared publicly. They have been viewed by the Cardano Foundation as administrator.\" The community is asked to rely on that attestation rather than on evidence.",
    "precedentDiscussion": "My Yes votes on Intersect's governance and technical stewardship and on the Blockfrost transformation funded work that Cardano itself runs on. My No votes on actions 158 and 161 held treasury withdrawals to evidence rather than promises and to funding public goods rather than private delivery. My DRep registration commits me to hold proposals \"to evidence rather than promises\". This vote follows that line.",
    "counterargumentDiscussion": "It is open source public infrastructure. The reusable open source core is a genuine public good and could be funded as one, and the proposal already routes a fifth of future verification revenue to core library maintenance. But the funded outcome here is a deployment for one state's police, delivered by a vendor that keeps the maintenance contract, with the state committed to pay for operation. The public good does not require the treasury to pay the commercial build.\n\nThe Cardano Foundation administers the funds, the price is capped and most future revenue returns. That governs oversight, overpayment and upside, not the core objection: the treasury pays a build the paying client could fund, at a figure not tied to the cost of the work, with most of the money released before the only milestone tied to use.\n\nThe team has a track record. Its ability to deliver is not what I question. The question is who pays for a commercial build and who carries the risk that it is built and not used.\n\nWhat would change my vote: a cost basis tied to rates and quantity of work, milestones tied to real adoption rather than to delivery, the client that has committed to pay for operation bearing the build cost, and the treasury funding only the reusable open source core at a verifiable price.",
    "conclusion": "BKIND votes No: 9,600,000 ada for a vendor to build and deliver a state government's own system, at a figure not tied to the cost of the work and with most of the money released before the only milestone tied to use, is the commons carrying a private commercial delivery (govActionId 72491608dc1a500d38613214069a2bd3b7e9a0e670d5abd7d6374e6bb54fc0e8#0).",
